    "body": "Seems good to me. So this would consist of moving what is currently steps 16 and 23 up to after step 9, I think? That is, we still want to:\r\n\r\n- Check \"cannot navigate\" (multiple times)\r\n- Check sandboxing\r\n- Fire submit events\r\n- Construct the entry list and thus fire formdata events\r\n\r\nBut we do not want to:\r\n\r\n- Bail early if the action=\"\" value is not parseable as a URL\r\n- Call \"[the rules for choosing a navigable](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-sequences.html#the-rules-for-choosing-a-navigable)\" including potentially creating a new window, consulting target/formtarget, etc.\r\n\r\nWould you be up for writing a spec PR and tests PR covering these?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
